{#- The frame of every turn of the Intel Phi Cortex chat model: the format it is trained in (tools/chat-text.c),
    <|system|>TEXT<|end|>, <|user|>TEXT<|end|>, <|assistant|>ANSWER<|end|>, each marker one token of the chat BPE
    (tools/bpe.c), a newline after each <|end|>. Variables: messages (role system | user | assistant, content),
    identity (name), add_generation_prompt. A system message, when given, comes first; without one, a short identity
    line stands in its place. The generation prompt is the assistant marker alone: the chat base's answers carry no
    think block (2026-10-27), and a model trained on data with reasoning opens its own <|think|> block, which the
    harness shows apart. Re-fed assistant turns carry no think block (the harness strips it, as Qwen's template
    does). The export `stop` lists the strings a reply ends before: the end marker, and every role marker, since a
    reply that begins the next turn has ended (the harness shows which). -#}
{%- set stop = ["<|end|>", "<|user|>", "<|system|>", "<|assistant|>"] -%}
{%- set name = identity.name | default("Cortex") -%}
{%- if messages | length == 0 or messages[0].role != "system" -%}
<|system|>I am {{ name }}.
I am a small language model on a Xeon Phi card.
I have one hundred and twenty columns.
I like to talk with people.<|end|>
{% endif -%}
{%- for m in messages -%}
{%- if m.role == "system" -%}
<|system|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% elif m.role == "user" -%}
<|user|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% else -%}
<|assistant|>{{ m.content | trim }}<|end|>
{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
<|assistant|>
{%- endif -%}
